# TRANSLATION

From wherever the mind wanders due to its flickering and unsteady nature, one must certainly withdraw it and bring it back under the control of the self.

# PURPORT

The nature of the mind is flickering and unsteady. But a self-realized yogé has to control the mind; the mind should not control him. One who controls the mind (and therefore the senses as well) is called gosvämé, or svämé, and one who is controlled by the mind is called go-däsa, or the servant of the senses.

